{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Method on Validator<D>.\n/// Encode the answer and atomically replace this source/criterion's record.\npub fn store_evidence<O: serde::Serialize>(\n    &self,\n    inputs: &Fingerprinted<D, O>,\n) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n```\n\nThe method saves under the source identity and criterion path captured in\n`Fingerprinted`, preserving its revision, input trace, and completed answer. Encoding follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`; atomic replacement follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. The result type needs\nno `Sync` bound: the method encodes the answer and captures the record and\nstorage key before constructing the storage future.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests check each obligation of `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.store_evidence`.\n\n**Save under the captured source and criterion path.**\n- `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` saves under the `behavior`, `structure` and `text` criteria of one source. It checks that each record sits under its own path, that `load_evidence` is `None` before a save, and that `store_evidence` is the step that writes.\n- `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors` in `tests/storage.rs` uses the non-trivial source id `\"opaque/é\"`. It stores through `Validator::store_evidence`, then reads the record straight from the domain at that source and criterion and finds the saved output. This shows the source identity and criterion path captured in `Fingerprinted` are the ones used.\n\n**Preserve revision, input trace and completed answer.**\n- `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` compares the loaded revision, dependencies, output and source node with the stored value.\n- `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` asserts that the saved record's dependencies are the `Dependency::Node` entry with the \"after\" fingerprint.\n- `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` checks that the saved revision and dependencies match the saved output.\n- `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` checks `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` in the stored record.\n- `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` checks that the restored record matches on every field.\n\n**Encoding.**\n- `serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged` stores an `Unencodable` answer over an existing record. It expects `ValidationError::Output`, an unchanged revision, dependencies and output, and no extra write.\n- `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments` makes storage fail and expects `ValidationError::Graph(\"store\")`, with no record written.\n- `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts the stored JSON shape of the output.\n\n**Atomic replacement.**\n- `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence` replaces an existing record with a new store. It then asserts exactly one record remains for the key.\n- `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` saves two competing records for one key with `join!`. It asserts one record remains, and that its revision, dependencies and output all come from the same save, in either order.\n\n**No `Sync` bound on the result type.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` stores a `Cell<u32>` answer, which is `Send` but not `Sync`. It passes `validator.store_evidence(&value)` through the `send` helper and unwraps the result, so the future is checked to be `Send`.\n\nThe cited requirements `record.output` and `evidence_storage` are context only. Their relevant behaviors are also exercised by the tests above.\n\nI found no unexercised obligation and no acknowledged gap.",
  "references": "fee20cda4b5cbc28c399ccdf5f82ec402a651edf604f0e0738ee3027b07d3c19",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.store_evidence",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.store_evidence"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} store_evidence",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "// Method on Validator<D>.",
        "/// Encode the answer and atomically replace this source/criterion's record.",
        "pub fn store_evidence<O: serde::Serialize>(",
        "    &self,",
        "    inputs: &Fingerprinted<D, O>,",
        ") -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;",
        "```",
        "",
        "The method saves under the source identity and criterion path captured in",
        "`Fingerprinted`, preserving its revision, input trace, and completed answer. Encoding follows",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`; atomic replacement follows",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. The result type needs",
        "no `Sync` bound: the method encodes the answer and captures the record and",
        "storage key before constructing the storage future.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} record.output",
        "`Validator::store_evidence` serializes the answer in `Fingerprinted` before passing",
        "the complete record to storage. A serialization failure returns",
        "`ValidationError::Output` and leaves the existing record unchanged. A storage",
        "failure returns `ValidationError::Graph`.",
        "",
        "`Validator::load_evidence` decodes a loaded record's output into the requested",
        "`Criterion::Ok`. An output that cannot decode returns `ValidationError::Output`,",
        "including when the saved revision or inputs are stale. Missing evidence returns",
        "`Ok(None)`; malformed stored records and storage failures return",
        "`ValidationError::Graph`. Revision and input comparison belong to the caller's",
        "reuse workflow under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.procedure_identity`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} evidence_storage",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`",
        "",
        "`trust_but_verify::Domain` provides evidence persistence for the",
        "{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`:",
        "",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "use std::future::Future;",
        "",
        "// Defined in trust_but_verify.",
        "pub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {",
        "    // ...",
        "",
        "    /// Ok(None) means absent; Err means loading failed.",
        "    fn load_evidence(",
        "        &self,",
        "        source: &Self::NodeId,",
        "        criterion: &CriterionPath,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<",
        "        Option<Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>>,",
        "        Self::Error,",
        "    >> + Send;",
        "",
        "    /// Atomically replace only this source/criterion pair's complete record.",
        "    fn store_evidence(",
        "        &self,",
        "        source: &Self::NodeId,",
        "        criterion: &CriterionPath,",
        "        record: &Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;",
        "",
        "    // ...",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "The validator passes the source identity and criterion path to both methods. The",
        "key preserves both parts: source paths `[\"a\"]` and `[\"a\", \"b\"]` with criteria",
        "`[\"b\", \"c\"]` and `[\"c\"]` identify different records, even though flattening each",
        "pair would produce the same segments.",
        "",
        "Different criteria of a source have independent records. A revision change",
        "invalidates the same criterion's record rather than creating another key.",
        "",
        "Successful loads observe either an old or new complete record, or absence",
        "before the first save. Successful competing saves leave one complete record;",
        "its revision, dependencies, and output all belong to that save. No ordering",
        "between competing saves is guaranteed.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
